## Session start (do this first, ~10s)

1. Refresh the shared AI files unless your harness already did (Claude Code's hook does):
   `bash ../AICodeFactory/sync-ai-templates.sh . --quiet --commit --pull --agents` (twin
   `.ps1`). Not a sibling → `$AI_CODE_ROOT/AICodeFactory` or the path in `~/.ai-template-dir`,
   never `~/Code`; not on this machine → say so once. Its copies belong to the template: never
   hand-edit them. Act on every `ai-sync:` line; `dev-context <name>` → read and follow
   `CLAUDE.local.md` (this code root's development rules; never another root's).
2. `git log --oneline -10` and `git status`. Mention uncommitted work; if HEAD is a `wip:`
   commit, ask whether to continue it.
3. Read `.github/PROJECT_STATE.md`; grep `.github/KNOWLEDGE.md` for the area, tool or error at
   hand — never read it whole. Line 1 of this file or those two still a bootstrap-pending
   marker → invoke the `bootstrap-ai` skill; don't hand-roll it.

